# Negative-control mutant — a pending contract is offered no SCHEDULE_FUTURE option (W1/B2, AC-11)
#
# Scenario it must flip: research.md:1496 names five eligibility conditions for
#   booking a future cancellation: product cancellation, NOT a pending contract,
#   no hard request, no existing scheduled request, an anniversary anchor. The
#   cancellation form's `option` enum is built from `cancellationOptions`
#   (contract-product.machine.ts:476), so the pending exclusion that governs what
#   a page can offer lives on that pure selector — NOT on the
#   useContractProduct.meta.ts convenience flag the previous version mutated,
#   which no schema reads (that is why it was inert).
# Test that goes red: contract-product.mutations.int.test.ts >
#   "AC-11 a product whose contract is pending is not offered SCHEDULE_FUTURE in
#   the cancellation form" — it overrides the recorded product's contract to
#   PENDING, opens the cancellation form, and asserts the schema's `option.enum`
#   does NOT contain SCHEDULE_FUTURE. Dropping `!isPending` from the
#   SCHEDULE_FUTURE branch pushes that option for the pending product, so the
#   enum now contains it and `expect(options).not.toContain(SCHEDULE_FUTURE)`
#   flips.
# Mutation: drops the `!isPending` guard from `cancellationOptions`'
#   SCHEDULE_FUTURE branch, reverting to the four-condition read that offers a
#   future-cancellation booking on a pending contract.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
index 088b7eca9..d8bccf14d 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ export function cancellationOptions(
     options.push(ContractProductCancelOption.HARD);
   }
   // SCHEDULE_FUTURE — needs a live subscription, no hard request, no scheduled cancellation and an anniversary anchor.
-  if (!isPending && !hasHard && !hasScheduled && !!anniversaryAnchor(product)) {
+  if (!hasHard && !hasScheduled && !!anniversaryAnchor(product)) {
     options.push(ContractProductCancelOption.SCHEDULE_FUTURE);
   }
 
